eceive a size class value when you read either the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EnvironmentValues\/horizontalSizeClass"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EnvironmentValues\/verticalSizeClass"},{"type":"text","text":" environment value. The value tells"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you about the amount of space available to your views in a given"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"direction. You can read the size class like any other of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", by creating a property with the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property wrapper:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Environment(\\.horizontalSizeClass) private var horizontalSizeClass","@Environment(\\.verticalSizeClass) private var verticalSizeClass"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"OpenSwiftUI sets the size class based on several factors, including:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The current device type.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The orientation of the device."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The appearance of Slide Over and Split View on iPad."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Several built-in views change their behavior based on the size class."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationView"},{"type":"text","text":" presents a multicolumn view when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text